#% title
# d_gaussian_wavelet

#% text
# `d_gaussian_wavelet(m)` is the m-th derivative of a Gaussian as a wavelet (default 2): in frequency -i^m/sqrt(gamma(m + 1/2)) (s w)^m exp(-(s w)^2/2) (Torrence and Compo, 1998, table 1).

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
x = n(table(sign(cos(k^2/100)), [k, 64]))

#% cell
wavelet_scalogram(continuous_wavelet_transform(x, d_gaussian_wavelet(5), [4, 2]))
